.PS
# Voltage-controlled sources in cascade: the 1:2 divider R1/R2 feeds a
# VCVS (gain 10, loaded by R3), whose output drives a VCCS (1 mS) into
# RL = 2k. Closed form: v(vx) = vin/2, v(vm) = 5 vin, v(vout) =
# -1m * 2k * v(vm) = -10 vin.
spice = 1
Vin:  (0.3,2)
Vx:   (1.6,2)
Vm:   (3,2)
Vout: (6.6,2)

V1: vsource((0.3,2), (0.3,0), DC 0)
R1: resistor((0.3,2), (1.6,2), 1k)
R2: resistor((1.6,2), (1.6,0), 1k)
E1: vcvs((3,2), (3,0), (2.5,1.2), (2.5,0.8), 10)
R3: resistor((4.1,2), (4.1,0), 1k)
G1: vccs((5.5,2), (5.5,0), (5,1.2), (5,0.8), 1m)
RL: resistor((6.6,2), (6.6,0), 2k)

line from Vx to (2.1,2) then to (2.1,1.2) then to E1.Cp
line from E1.Cn to (2.1,0.8) then to (2.1,0)
line from E1.P to R3.P then to (4.6,2) then to (4.6,1.2) then to G1.Cp
line from G1.Cn to (4.6,0.8) then to (4.6,0)
line from G1.P to RL.P
line from V1.N to RL.N
dot at Vx; dot at R3.P
dot at R2.N; dot at (2.1,0); dot at E1.N; dot at R3.N; dot at (4.6,0); dot at G1.N
ground(V1.N)
.dc V1 -1 1 0.5
.PE
